invariant: INV-19
file: sha512_avx2.c
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh sha512-stack
reason: sha512_avx2_compress_blocks keeps an array of eighty words beside
  its sums, the size of the reference's message schedule, writes a state
  word into it and reads the word back, so its frame is 640 bytes larger
  and passes the 512 bytes of stack sha512_hw.c wipes below each call of
  it (SHA512_AVX2_BELOW_LEN): the word stays in the dead frame. Every
  digest is right, and the frame is far inside the budget every other
  file of a host object holds. The file has a budget of its own,
  STACK_BUDGET_SHA512_AVX2, below that length, and make lint-stack-run for
  the TRUST=webpki object with SUITE=aesgcm fails on it. The kernel has a
  body on x86-64 alone, so the catch is the script, which runs that lint
  under gcc for x86-64 on every host before it builds a binary with
  clang; make check's check-stack-suite runs the same lint and compiles
  the kernel where its compiler targets x86-64. The edit reads the array
  because gcc refuses a variable that is only set, and the lane would
  then stop at the kernel's compile and never run the lint. The lane
  skips without docker, and this then reports unguarded rather than
  caught.

--- old
    _Alignas(32) uint64_t sums[16];
    for (; blocks > 0; blocks--) {
--- new
    _Alignas(32) uint64_t sums[16];
    volatile uint64_t schedule[80];
    schedule[blocks % 80] = state[0];
    state[0] = schedule[blocks % 80];
    for (; blocks > 0; blocks--) {
